 $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,1,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424230 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df216990-7a71-5841-8a5b-955dc6939d8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424230 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+y)^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}((y+z)^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+z)^{2}) \\\\  & =2(x+y)+2(y+z)+2(x+z) \\\\  & =4(x+y+z).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,1,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F(-2,1,-1) & =4((-2)+(1)+(-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1045 "Row and Column Operations on Determinants" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186424902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424892 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "11b6f742-f965-5993-a06f-bca8dfba7485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424893 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424893 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/re